---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <h1>👋 Hello, World!</h1>
      <p>
        Welcome to the official <a href="https://restacked.ai/">Restacked</a> demo
        template. This template serves as a lightweight, minimally-styled starting
        point for anyone looking to build a static website with a blog on Restacked
        platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        This template is built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, a
        modern static site generator that allows you to build fast,
        content-focused websites using your favorite frontend frameworks. You
        can easily add
        <a href="https://astro.build/integrations">Astro Integrations</a> to add tools
        like Tailwind, React, or Vue to your project.
      </p>
      <h2>Features</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>✅ Minimal styling (make it your own!)</li>
        <li>✅ 100/100 Lighthouse performance</li>
        <li>✅ SEO-friendly with canonical URLs and OpenGraph data</li>
        <li>✅ Sitemap support</li>
        <li>✅ RSS Feed support</li>
        <li>✅ Markdown support</li>
        <li>✅ DecapCMS for easy content editing</li>
        <li>✅ Cloudinary for image hosting and optimization</li>
        <li>✅ GitHub Actions for automated deployment to GitHub Pages</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Here are a few ideas on how to get started with the demo template:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Edit this page in <code>src/pages/index.astro</code></li>
        <li>
          Edit the site header items in <code>src/components/Header.astro</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          Add your name to the footer in <code>src/components/Footer.astro</code
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          Customize the blog post page layout in <code
            >src/layouts/BlogPost.astro</code
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          Edit blog posts in <a href="/demo/admin">the admin panel</a> powered by
          <a href="https://decapcms.org/">DecapCMS</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
